// Landflow plugin protocol — v1
//
// A plugin is a process that hosts one or more node types. The Landflow host
// discovers plugins, pulls their manifest, renders the node UI from the
// descriptors and calls Execute when a workflow reaches one of their nodes.
//
// The same contract is exposed over HTTP+JSON (see docs/protocol.md). Anything
// recursive or open-ended (node descriptors, parameters, item payloads) travels
// as a JSON-encoded DynamicValue so both transports share one JSON Schema
// (packages/protocol/schema/*.json). This mirrors Terraform's tfplugin
// DynamicValue approach: a typed envelope, a dynamic payload.

